# Black Lotus is an artifact spell before it is an ability: cast on turn 3 it can be countered. Bot2 (Mox Sapphire and an
# Island, played on turn 2) counters it with Counterspell, so it goes from the stack to the graveyard unsacrificed and
# never produces mana. The mana ability itself is not on the stack, so it cannot be responded to once it is on the
# battlefield (the control is every other Lotus scenario).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Black Lotus)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Mana =
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
